Surfaced by k21 (compiler.js suite). Lib::async_for (lib/Text/Nunjucks/Lib.pm ~line 296) fetches loop values with a raw $obj->{$k} hash-deref. A template dict literal and any caller-supplied ordered hash is a blessed Hash::Ordered (ADR 0011), not a plain hashref, so it dies "Not a HASH reference". Only affects {% asyncEach %}/{% asyncAll %} object/dict iteration (Runtime::async_each -> Lib::async_for non-array branch); plain {% for %} iterates such values fine. 6 TODO subtests in t/upstream/compiler.t pin it. Fix: read ordered-hash members via ->get/->keys (mirror the member_lookup/keys ordered branches). Reproduce via the TODO subtests, then add a corpus render case.

Re-claiming after k42. k41 needs BOTH Lib::async_for AND Runtime::async_all Hash::Ordered branches (previous worker only fixed Lib::async_for; Runtime::async_all does its own direct $arr->{$k} deref). Stale claim released.

